message: "If you use or build on Bucketization, please cite it as below."
title: "Bucketization: fast re-sorting of multi-column views by per-key bucket assignment"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Attila"
    family-names: "Torda"
repository-code: "https://github.com/attilatorda/SpeedUp"
url: "https://github.com/attilatorda/SpeedUp/blob/v0.2.0/docs/bucketization/README.md"
version: "v0.2.0"
date-released: "2026-10-27"
license: AGPL-3.0-only
keywords:
  - sorting
  - bucket sort
  - file manager
  - multi-key sort
  - incremental sorting
abstract: >-
  Bucketization keeps, for every sort key of a collection (for example name,
  size and modification time in a file manager), a bucket assignment per
  element, with page-sized buckets at both ends. Switching the sort key or
  direction regroups the elements in linear time and sorts only the buckets
  that are on screen; groupings are cached per key, and groups keep folders
  first in both directions.
